      "A truck carries the bin's contents to a sorting center. There, machines and workers separate paper, metal cans, glass, and different kinds of plastic. Most water bottles are made of a plastic called PET, which is marked with the number 1 inside a small triangle of arrows. The sorted bottles are crushed and pressed into giant bundles called bales.",
      "From Bottles to Pellets",
      "The bales are shipped to a recycling plant, where the bottles go through several steps:\n1. They are washed, and the caps and labels are removed.\n2. They are chopped into tiny flakes.\n3. The flakes are melted and shaped into pellets about the size of a grain of rice.",
      "A New Product",
      "Factories buy the pellets and melt them again to make new things. Some become new bottles. Others are spun into thread for carpets and soft, warm fleece jackets. A bottle you threw away could someday keep someone warm on a winter day.",
